<BaseLayout title="About & Editorial Method" description="How Dama Korea researches, drafts, illustrates, reviews and updates its independent Korean heritage field guides." activeNav="/about/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell visual-shell"><div><p class="eyebrow">About Dama Korea</p><h1>Independent field guides, with the method left visible.</h1><p class="page-hero__lede">Dama Korea publishes English-language guidance for understanding and visiting Korean heritage under a clearly disclosed house publishing name.</p></div></div></section>
  <article class="legal-shell article-body">
    <h2>What the name means</h2><p>Dama Korea is the house publishing name used for this website. The name is not a person or team, and it does not identify a government body, heritage authority, museum, religious organization, travel agency or other official institution.</p><p>Guides are published under the Dama Korea byline. The site does not claim personal visits, professional qualifications or privileged access. It does not invent a traveler, biography, quotation, interview or first-person experience to create authority.</p>
    <h2>What makes a field guide useful</h2><p>Official pages can confirm an opening notice or define a monument, but a visitor still needs to choose a route, recognize what matters and prepare for points of failure. Dama Korea’s original value comes from that synthesis: comparisons, spatial explanations, annotated sequences and reusable decision tools.</p>
    <h2>Research and source roles</h2><p>Each guide begins with the organization responsible for the site or rule. Historical interpretation is checked against appropriate heritage institutions, museums and specialist sources. Factual and time-sensitive claims are checked against the linked sources named in each guide, and every source is labeled with the claim or decision it supports.</p>
    <h2>How AI-assisted tools are used</h2><p>AI-assisted tools help organize research, support drafting and create original SVG editorial schematics. They are not treated as sources. These tools are not used to fabricate a visit, quotation, interview, contributor identity or qualification.</p>
    <h2>What the current visuals are</h2><p>The current SVG visuals are AI-assisted editorial schematics created for Dama Korea. They are not photographs, measured maps, historical reconstructions or evidence of current on-site conditions. Captions state their interpretive purpose and limits.</p>
    <h2>Publication gate</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>The guide solves one defined visitor or interpretation problem.</li><li>Historical and time-sensitive claims use sources appropriate to their role.</li><li>The page adds an original route, comparison, diagram, observation framework or decision tool.</li><li>Visual rights, accessibility text and captions are complete.</li><li>Dates and material changes are recorded honestly.</li><li>Draft, empty and unverified pages remain outside the public build.</li></ul>
    <h2>Corrections and current commercial status</h2><p>Readers can use the <a href="/contact/">public corrections channel</a> to identify a changed source or unclear passage. The site currently uses only an AdSense ownership-verification meta tag and <code>ads.txt</code>. It does not load AdSense JavaScript or display Google-served ads, and it has no affiliate links, sponsored content or paid placements.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
